    "title": "What channel is Gonzaga vs. Texas on? Time, TV schedule, live stream to watch March Madness Round 2 game",
    "text": "What channel is Gonzaga vs. Texas on? Time, TV schedule, live stream to watch March Madness Round 2 game originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.AdvertisementThe second round of the 2026 NCAA Tournament continues on Saturday, March 21, as No. 3 Gonzaga takes on No. 11 Texas.Gonzaga took on No. 14 Kennesaw State in the first round of the tournament and won 73-64 in a game that Kennesaw State kept close throughout. Texas was one of the last four teams in and actually had a play-in game to become the No. 11 seed. The Longhorns beat NC State and then upset BYU to make the second round.Gonzaga was led in scoring by Graham Ike, who had 19 points. The 7-foot Matas Vokietatis was the leading scorer for Texas in its win, dropping 23 points and adding 16 rebounds. The matchup of the big men down low will be one to watch in this game, with both serving as their respective team's star.Here's what you need to know about Saturday's matchup between Gonzaga vs. Texas, including broadcast information and start time.AdvertisementTV channel: TBS, truTVGonzaga and Texas will square off in the second round of the 2026 NCAA Tournament. Their game on Saturday will air on TBS and truTV. The game's announcers will be Brad Nessler, Wally Szczerbiak and Jared Greenberg.Fans looking to stream Gonzaga vs. Texas can watch live on DIRECTV.Catch every game of March Madness — try DIRECTV FREE today! Stream live Soccer, MLB, and more with must-have sports channels like TNT, TBS, truTV, ESPN, FS1, and NFL Network—all included with DIRECTV.Start your FREE trial now and never miss a moment of the action. No contracts, no hassle, just wall-to-wall sports and entertainment.AdvertisementWhat time is Gonzaga vs. Texas today?Date: Saturday, March 21Time: 7:10 p.m. ETThe NCAA tournament game between Gonzaga and. Texas is set to tip off at 7:10 p.m. ET from the Moda Center in Portland, Oregon.Gonzaga made the NCAA Tournament for the first time in 1995 and has been a powerhouse ever since, making the tourney in 27 straight years. The first time they made the Big Dance, they lost in the first round. Gonzaga is looking to make the Sweet Sixteen for the seventh time in the last eight tournaments.Texas has made the NCAA Tournament for the fourth year in a row. Most recently, the Longhorns lost in their first four matchup in 2025, and are hoping to reach the Sweet Sixteen for the first time since 2023.AdvertisementGonzaga vs. Texas radio coverageListen to every game of the 2026 NCAA men's basketball tournament live on SiriusXM.New subscribers can listen to SiriusXM for free for four months. Listen to live NFL, MLB, NBA and NHL games, plus NASCAR, college sports and more. Stay updated with all the news and get all the analysis on multiple sport-specific channels.March Madness bracket 2026Check the Sporting News NCAA Tournament live bracket for the latest final scores and next-round matchups.When and where is the Final Four in 2026?Date: April 4 and 6Location: Lucas Oil Stadium, IndianapolisThe 2026 Men's Final Four is set for April 4 and 6 at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis. The semifinals will be played Saturday night and the national championship game is set for Monday night.AdvertisementThe home of the Indianapolis Colts previously hosted the event in 2010, 2015 and 2021 and is set to host again in 2029. Indianapolis previously hosted the Final Four at other facilities in 1980, 1991, 1997, 2000 and 2006.Only Kansas City has been home to the Final Four more often (10 times), but the last one held there was in 1988.March Madness tournament schedule 2026Here is the round-by-round schedule for the 2026 NCAA men’s basketball tournament:RoundDateFirst roundMarch 19-20Second roundMarch 21-22Sweet 16March 26-27Elite EightMarch 28-29Final FourApril 4National championshipApril 6Related Links",
